From: MahanHD <mahanheidari2003@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] slimbus: qcom-ngd: let the slaves go without holding tx_lock

When the ADSP shuts down, the SSR notifier took tx_lock and, still
holding it, unregistered the controller. That removes every slave, and a
slave's remove path can transfer: removing the WCD9320 codec tears down
its sound card, which waits for userspace to close the PCM, and the close
powers DAPM down with register writes. Each write blocked on tx_lock,
the card waited for the close, and the notifier waited for the card. An
ADSP restart with the codec loaded hung in D state for good.

Take tx_lock only to wait out the transfer in flight and mark the
controller down, remove the slaves without it, and take it again to free
the DMA. A transfer made once the QMI link to the manager is gone fails
at once instead of timing out against an ADSP that is not there.

---
--- a/drivers/slimbus/qcom-ngd-ctrl.c
+++ b/drivers/slimbus/qcom-ngd-ctrl.c
@@ -798,6 +798,10 @@
 	u8 la = txn->la;
 	bool usr_msg = false;
 
+	/* no QMI link to the manager: it is going down, nothing can answer */
+	if (!ctrl->qmi.handle)
+		return -ENODEV;
+
 	if (txn->mt == SLIM_MSG_MT_CORE &&
 		(txn->mc >= SLIM_MSG_MC_BEGIN_RECONFIGURATION &&
 		 txn->mc <= SLIM_MSG_MC_RECONFIGURE_NOW))
@@ -1531,12 +1535,23 @@
 	case SERVREG_SERVICE_STATE_DOWN:
 		/* Make sure the last dma xfer is finished */
 		mutex_lock(&ctrl->tx_lock);
-		if (ctrl->state != QCOM_SLIM_NGD_CTRL_DOWN) {
-			pm_runtime_get_noresume(ctrl->ctrl.dev);
-			ctrl->state = QCOM_SLIM_NGD_CTRL_DOWN;
-			qcom_slim_ngd_down(ctrl);
-			qcom_slim_ngd_exit_dma(ctrl);
+		if (ctrl->state == QCOM_SLIM_NGD_CTRL_DOWN) {
+			mutex_unlock(&ctrl->tx_lock);
+			break;
 		}
+		pm_runtime_get_noresume(ctrl->ctrl.dev);
+		ctrl->state = QCOM_SLIM_NGD_CTRL_DOWN;
+		mutex_unlock(&ctrl->tx_lock);
+
+		/*
+		 * Not under tx_lock: this unregisters the controller, and the
+		 * slaves' remove paths transfer (a codec's card teardown writes
+		 * its registers). Holding the lock deadlocked them.
+		 */
+		qcom_slim_ngd_down(ctrl);
+
+		mutex_lock(&ctrl->tx_lock);
+		qcom_slim_ngd_exit_dma(ctrl);
 		mutex_unlock(&ctrl->tx_lock);
 		break;
 	case QCOM_SSR_AFTER_POWERUP:
